// CLOSED 2026-09-23 (squeue #281): a `&Struct` param rebound to a spill slot by `&x` is registered as a slot-holding reference, and get_struct_ptr loads such a slot.
// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row param_ref_struct_cast_after_addr_of_reads_slot_run (tier 1). WRONG VALUE AT RUN TIME.
// `h(&x) == x as *const D` with `x: &D` a PARAMETER: MLIRGenImpl::gen_expr_kind(EAddrOfView)'s parameter arm spills `x` and REBINDS
// scope_[x] to the slot (ref_param_names_ erased), and the `x as *const D` cast that follows in the same block reads scope_[x] raw — the
// emitted `icmp eq %1, %0` compares h's answer with the SLOT, not %arg0: exit 1. The cast placed before `&x` is right (exit 0), and a
// read after `&x` in a sibling branch is right (the arm's scope restore undoes the rebind). Rust: exit 0.
// NEIGHBOUR of 2026-09-15d-argrefland's class (the same consumer, the parameter arm), ROWED, REASON 1 (the fact has no carrier there):
// EAddrOfView carries no mutability, so the arm cannot ask whether the rebind (the `&mut p` write-through route) is needed; the strict
// extension at the same site (register the slot's `&Struct` shape after the rebind) was built and measured: this program 1 -> 1, its
// generic and field-read variants 8 -> 8 and 3 -> 3. Measured on build-dev0915d. Legality MEASURED with rustc 1.98.1 (foot of this file).
package param_ref_struct_cast_after_addr_of_reads_slot_run;
struct D { v: i64 }
fn h(a: &&D) -> *const D {
    let x: &D = *a;
    return x as *const D;
}
fn g(x: &D) -> bool {
    return h(&x) == x as *const D;
}
fn main() -> i32 {
    let d: D = D { v: 6i64 };
    if !g(&d) { return 1i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
// rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 (round 2026-09-15f-rustcaudit, class CONFIRMED): COMPILES and RUNS exit 0. Twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15f-rustcaudit/rust/param_ref_struct_cast_after_addr_of_reads_slot_run.rs. Variants: param_ref_struct_cast_after_addr_of_reads_slot_run__copy.rs compiles, exit 0. Audit note: h(&x) == x as *const D compares the pointee address; control (another address) exit 1.
